summary:
  The helper no longer tells an Ogg stream with FLAC inside from one with
  Vorbis or Opus, so no station is ever sent to the relay on its answer.

history:
  An Ogg FLAC stream freezes 278 ms in when the player reads it off the
  socket and has to start through the relay; Vorbis and Opus in the same
  container do not. The directory files all three as OGG, so the first
  packet of the first page is the only place that says which it is.

target:
  package/contents/ui/streamkind.py

find:
      if packet[:5] == b"\x7fFLAC" or packet[:4] == b"fLaC":

replace:
      if packet[:5] == b"\x7fFLAX" or packet[:4] == b"fLaX":

expect:
  Killed by tests/test_streamkind.py::test_the_three_kinds_and_everything_else.
  Line-neutral.
